  "formalized_scope": [
    "Executable continuation recursion follows the false-first branch order and returns the same verdict and counted visits as short-circuiting the eager sequence, for any predicate and any variable list including duplicate IDs.",
    "The counted result erases to the uncounted search and its bound charges at most one solver invocation per candidate, up to 2^k.",
    "The mixed guard solver uses the bounded precomputed-guard constructor, proved equivalent at every leaf. The parent negative-ID list is constructed once per accepted call and captured by the branch predicate.",
    "Both optimized public decision entry points are exactly equivalent to the frozen eager solver. They inherit SAT and UNSAT correctness and preserve rejected mixed inputs. General CNF never rejects.",
    "The compiled search and public solver modules contain no enumerateBits call. Right continuations are built only after a false left result. The independent eagerCount exists for proof comparison and is unused by the actual solver."
